From f0052db0c795846aad5caa0367861d5e4fdc9113 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:33:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Voices, what a reader sees: the Voice row and sheet, and
 Listen on every text (held for his yes)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Build 95 note 25, his "all recs" of 2026-11-13: the phone's own voices, free
for every reader, reading the whole Bible, the lives, the councils, history,
theology and the Fathers' works; never the prayers. Held as a patch for his yes
on the stills (docs/handoffs/updates-17.md); applied on his word.

- The Voice row in the player's ••• (between Sleep timer and Ambience), its
  value the voice reading; a new mark, components/ui/icons/Voice.tsx.
- The Voice sheet (components/player/VoiceSheet.tsx), from the player's own
  parts, mounted once in the root frame: Heart first where the text has its
  recording, then the phone's voices for the text's language, each its name
  over its language, with Hear it (the first words of the verse being read, in
  that voice); choosing reads on in it at the verse being read. A chosen voice
  gone is said; a language with no voice and no recording says where a voice
  is added.
- Listen on every chapter where the device can speak (the Old Testament, a
  downloaded Bible's page in its own language and words), the verse lit where
  it stands, rolling on into the next chapter, previous and next opening the
  chapter's page; never over a licensed translation. ListenHere reads the
  page's paragraphs from its part on, in the page's language, the paragraph
  lit and its sentence washed. Never on a prayer's page.
- Ten strings in all 21 catalogs.

Tests that fail on the old code: lib/listen/speech/__tests__/voiceSheet.test.ts
(8); eight source-reading tests moved to the new rules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VuYTwZshCrYvNwoUyAX6F4
